# Modified in this fork (taehee-pd/harperSwift): `will` must follow its subject. In questions
# such as `Will going to the doctor help?` or `What will going to college teach me?`, the gerund
# `going to ...` is the subject, so nothing is redundant.
expr redundant [(will gonna), (will going to)]
expr notSubject [what, who, whom, which, whose, why, how, where, when, the, a, an, her, his, its, my, your, our, their]
expr main <(!@notSubject @redundant), ([NOUN, PRON, PROPN] @redundant), @redundant>

let message "`Will` already marks the future, so `gonna` or `going to` is redundant here."
let description "Corrects the redundant `will gonna` and `will going to` to `will`."
let kind "Redundancy"
let becomes "will"

# True positives
test "If it was urlencoded to put '%7c' instead of '|', it will gonna be ok." "If it was urlencoded to put '%7c' instead of '|', it will be ok."
test "When I change my category it will gonna submit my query instantly." "When I change my category it will submit my query instantly."
test "so once you press on the text/button near it, the app will gonna open the tab" "so once you press on the text/button near it, the app will open the tab"
test "We will going to develop multiple long running workflow for employees to request a vacation" "We will develop multiple long running workflow for employees to request a vacation"
test "on launch time it will going to crash" "on launch time it will crash"
test "Sarah will gonna call you later." "Sarah will call you later."
test "The server will going to restart at midnight." "The server will restart at midnight."
test "They will gonna love it!" "They will love it!"
test "I think she will going to win, but I'm not sure." "I think she will win, but I'm not sure."
test "THE BUILD WILL GONNA FAIL." "THE BUILD WILL FAIL."
test "You Will Going To Like This" "You Will Like This"

# False positives / true negatives
allows "It is going to rain, and it will rain tomorrow too."
allows "I'm gonna say it will work."
allows "Will going to the doctor help?"
allows "will going to bed early fix my sleep?"
allows "And will going to the gym every day really help?"
allows "Will gonna be accepted in formal writing?"
allows "The will going to probate surprised the family."
allows "What will going to college teach me?"
allows "We will be going to the park tomorrow."
allows "She will keep going to class."
